WEBVTT

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:29.670
I'm off.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.760
Wait, Hiromi.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:35.580
What, Mom?

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.220
"What?" I'm talking about your bicycle.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.600
You haven't ridden it since you were little.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.180
Are you sure you can ride that?

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.040
I'll be fine.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:47.780
They say it's muscle memory, right?

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.170
Riding a bike is easy.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:51.060
But...

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:54.150
Don't worry. I'll practice.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.110
That's why I'm leaving early.

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:57.800
Are you sure you're okay?

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.460
I'll be fine.

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:05.930
<i>I'm Maiharu Hiromi.</i>

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.560
<i>I moved to Kamakura from Nagasaki.</i>

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:10.170
Have a nice day.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:13.880
<i>Starting today, I'm a first-year 
at Minami Kamakura High school.</i>

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:19.130
<i>A new uniform, a new city, and...</i>

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:32.060
<i>...a new day's about to begin.</i>

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:09.160
<b>#1  Entrance Ceremony!</b>

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:11.310
Okay.

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:34.510
Oh, right. Bicycles don't move forward 
unless you turn these things, right?

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:40.490
This should make it move forward.

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:53.540
This station really is picturesque.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.790
It was worth walking from one station over.

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:02.280
S-Someone stop me!

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.640
Brake! Hit the brakes!

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.410
Oh, right.

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:17.000
Ouch...

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:18.980
Are you okay?

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:24.980
Sorry for bothering you.

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:27.000
Don't worry about it.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.050
I'm glad you don't seem too badly injured.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:29.950
That's good.

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:34.560
Are you a new student 
at Minami Kamakura High?

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:37.090
Huh? Yeah, I am.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:38.920
Are you a student there, too?

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.300
Yeah. I'm Akitsuki Tomoe.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:43.380
Tomoe...

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.370
Tomo-chan, then.

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:48.240
I'm Maiharu Hiromi. You can call me Hiromi.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:49.970
Nice to meet you, Hiromi.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:52.020
Nice to meet you, Tomo-chan.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:55.740
Anyway, is that bicycle broken?

00:04:55.740 --> 00:05:01.480
Oh, no. The problem lies somewhere else.

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:10.120
Um, apparently I've forgotten 
how to ride a bicycle.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:10.870
What?

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:16.860
Um, I'm not sure what you mean...

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:20.520
But you made it down the hill
 despite your wobbling.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.170
With some practice, you could 
probably learn to ride again.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:26.850
You're right.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:28.990
I need to at least know 
how to ride a bicycle.

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:30.480
What? Uh, y-yeah...

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:32.470
Since that's decided, I should practice.

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:33.750
Please help me.

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.390
What? Help you?

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:36.100
Me?

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:41.200
<i>Why is this happening?</i>

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:47.400
<i>Well, there's still some time 
before the entrance ceremony.</i>

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.370
<i>I can do this for a little bit.</i>

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:52.390
Here we go, Hiromi.

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:53.330
Okay.

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:56.410
There.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.400
Hiromi! Pedal, pedal!

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:06.300
No! Face forward!

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:13.830
Ouch...

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:17.460
Yikes. This might be difficult.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:20.400
Hiromi, pedal harder!

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:25.110
Your shoulders are stiff!

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:28.060
Don't try to balance yourself 
using the handlebars!

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:31.820
Face forward! Forward!

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:38.160
You're forgetting to pedal again!

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:47.710
There must be

00:06:48.370 --> 00:06:52.920
people on this Earth who are genetically 
incapable of riding bikes.

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:54.640
And I must be one of them.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:55.680
Hello?

00:06:55.680 --> 00:07:01.180
I'm not very good at anything, but I haven't 
been this bad at something in a while!

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:03.400
<i>She said it!</i>

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:06.210
That's enough, Tomo-chan.

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:08.900
The entrance ceremony is starting.

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:11.900
I can't ask you to keep practicing with me.

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:14.560
L-Let's try one more time.

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:15.460
What?

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:18.610
You've tried this hard already.

00:07:18.610 --> 00:07:22.500
It's okay. I'll hold you, okay?

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.460
Bicycles move forward as long as you pedal.

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:28.140
They'll move forward without falling.

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:32.220
Okay. Let's do it, Tomo-chan.

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:37.920
I'm ready back here, Hiromi.

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:42.060
Okay. Here we go.

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:47.240
That's it. Keep pedaling.

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:50.040
I'm doing it. I'm doing it, Tomo-chan!

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:52.540
Yeah, you're pretty steady now.

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:54.870
Hiromi, I'm letting go.

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:55.740
What?

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:57.110
Go!

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:15.700
I'm doing it.

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:18.360
I'm riding a bicycle.

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:19.860
Wow.

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:23.980
Yeah, that's it!

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.030
I did it, Tomo-chan!

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:36.920
Yeah, that's amazing!

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:42.430
I managed to ride my bike.

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:47.310
Yeah, but it's still too dangerous 
for you to go out on the road.

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:49.660
Yeah. What should we do?

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:53.090
I think there are bike racks 
near the station.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:57.380
They're full.

00:08:57.380 --> 00:08:58.660
Oh, my.

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:01.200
What should we do, Captain Tomoe?

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:04.770
We can't just abandon your bike somewhere.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:08.150
Let's push your bike to school.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:13.890
Hiromi, you moved here from Nagasaki?

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:16.480
Yeah, I just came here.

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:18.450
What do you think of Kamakura?

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:22.710
Well, there are a lot of hills.

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:24.750
And at the bottom of those hills are beaches.

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:27.190
It's sort of like Nagasaki.

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:29.670
Oh, really?

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:37.010
Tomo-chan, is the school much farther?

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:40.470
Yeah, about 15 minutes.

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:44.640
What? But I'm tired.

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:46.380
You can do it.

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:49.290
If you're too slow, we won't 
make the entrance ceremony.

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:54.320
And you'll get to see something 
nice once we turn that corner.

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:55.350
What?

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.850
Wow!

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:12.400
This is one of Kamakura's ocean views?

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:27.310
Wow, there are lots of little suns.

00:10:28.490 --> 00:10:29.940
You're right.

00:10:31.010 --> 00:10:32.490
It's so pretty.

00:10:34.090 --> 00:10:34.970
Hiromi...

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:35.940
Huh?

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:38.030
Welcome to Kamakura.

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:39.910
We're glad to have you.

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:44.550
Thanks, Tomo-chan.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:08.130
What a pleasant breeze.

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:12.520
This is the best road for cycling.

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:19.780
Anyway, I wonder where 
Minami Kamakura High is?

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:21.780
<b>Enoshima Station</b>

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:21.780
<b>Minami
 Kamakura High</b>

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:21.780
<b>My Shop</b>

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:21.780
<b>Eat Up</b>

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:21.780
<b>Ocean</b>

00:11:22.190 --> 00:11:26.330
The map Nagisa gave me isn't 
specific enough, so I have no idea.

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:29.430
Did I bike past it?

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:32.810
This feels great.

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:35.450
The smell of sea breeze 
is so refreshing, too.

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:37.580
I've always lived in Kamakura.

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:39.380
I don't know much about other beaches,

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:42.410
but it might mean our beaches are 
just that clean and beautiful.

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:43.840
Wow.

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:48.100
Hey, Tomo-chan. Is that mountain...

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:49.970
Yeah, it's Mt. Fuji.

00:11:49.970 --> 00:11:53.020
Wow! It's just like the
Mt. Fuji I've seen in photos.

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:55.610
Of course.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:59.110
I've never seen Mt. Fuji in person before.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:01.740
It looks so close.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:04.640
From here, we're about 70 kilometers away.

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:09.060
By the way, Enoshima is to the left, 
and in front of it is Shichirigahama.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:10.780
Really?

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:15.560
Oh, we get a lot of black kites around here.

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:18.630
Be careful whenever you're eating.

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:23.210
They'll mercilessly take things 
right out of a person's hands.

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:25.090
Hey, students!

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:26.470
Wait up!

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:27.620
Who is that?

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:28.420
Who knows?

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:32.680
You're students from
Minami Kamakura, aren't you?

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:37.150
Y-Yes. Actually, I'm about to become one...

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:38.990
I knew it.

00:12:38.990 --> 00:12:42.410
Then you know where the school is, right?

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:44.110
Could you give me directions?

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:47.600
What? Well, actually...

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:48.750
That's it right there.

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:49.330
What?

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:53.040
Oh? I can't believe it was
right in front of me.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:56.040
That's good. We're finally here.

00:12:56.540 --> 00:13:00.080
<i>Is she a teacher?</i>

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:02.760
What was that sound?

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:07.590
I got up early this morning,
so I didn't get to eat breakfast.

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:08.820
But it's okay.

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:12.430
My mom made me sandwiches.

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:14.880
Thanks for the food.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.800
Hiromi, don't!

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:17.570
Why? Tomo-chan, do you want some?

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:19.100
That's not what I meant.

00:13:19.100 --> 00:13:20.470
You don't want any?

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:30.470
My sandwich!

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:32.880
I told you to watch out for the kites.

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:32.880
Hey, give it back!

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:35.370
They've taken my food plenty of times.

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.830
It's fine. I have another one.

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:38.750
What?

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:39.330
They're coming.

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:44.140
Hiromi, put that away!

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:45.880
Okay, I'll eat it right away!

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:47.890
That's not what I said! Put it away!

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:51.110
I won't let the kites take it from me!

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:55.250
You two, run to the school!

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:57.100
Yes, ma'am!

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:07.410
Give me a break.

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:08.910
Sorry, sorry.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:12.740
Minami Kamakura High...

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:17.360
Starting today, we'll be attending 
school here for three years.

00:14:17.360 --> 00:14:18.120
Yeah.

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:21.590
But there's nobody here.

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:24.750
Everyone's already gone 
to the entrance ceremony.

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:27.090
What? Is it already that time?

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:28.670
We should go, too.

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:34.450
Before that, you should check the 
board for your class assignments.

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:35.840
Oh, right.

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:37.390
Tomo-chan, it's over there.

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:39.280
Hurry, Hiromi!

00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:40.740
Wait, Tomo-chan!

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:41.970
Hurry up!

00:14:41.970 --> 00:14:43.440
Okay!

00:14:41.970 --> 00:14:44.730
Good grief. What a noisy couple of students.

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:49.360
I found mine.

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:51.340
<b>Maiharu Hiromi</b>

00:14:49.810 --> 00:14:51.340
I'm in class B.

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:53.280
<b>First-Year Class B: Akitsuki Tomoe</b>

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:53.280
I'm in class B, too.

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:57.080
I look forward to spending 
the year with you, Hiromi.

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:59.080
Yeah, Tomo-chan.

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:04.980
<i>New students, welcome 
to Minami Kamakura High.</i>

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:10.490
<i>As students who are now members of a 
high school in historical Kamakura,</i>

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:12.860
<i>I welcome you from the bottom of my heart.</i>

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:20.690
<i>Today you will begin your life as 
students of Minami Kamakura High.</i>

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:23.460
<i>The great difference between those of you 
who were middle schoolers until March,</i>

00:15:22.010 --> 00:15:25.720
<i>All of these people are my classmates.</i>

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:27.670
<i>and those of you lining up here 
is your personal desire to study.</i>

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:30.110
<i>Even after finishing compulsory education,</i>

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:31.780
<i>There are lots of smart-looking 
people and athletic-looking people.</i>

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:31.780
<i>you chose on your own to study at our school.</i>

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:34.070
<i>Is that a foreigner?</i>

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:34.920
<i>The three years you spend 
here will not go smoothly.</i>

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:39.910
<i>You will experience painful times and times 
that make you want to give up on everything.</i>

00:15:36.170 --> 00:15:39.910
<i>Will I be able to make friends?</i>

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:41.110
<i>That's right.</i>

00:15:41.110 --> 00:15:42.390
<i>I'm in a strange place.</i>

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:44.390
<i>I don't know anybody.</i>

00:15:44.390 --> 00:15:47.550
<i>Will I spend my high school life alone?</i>

00:15:48.180 --> 00:15:53.050
<i>I'll eat my lunches in the bathroom 
and won't find partners for PE class.</i>

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:55.010
<i>Someday, I'll even fail my classes,</i>

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:56.830
<i>and then I'll begin refusing
to come to school.</i>

00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:58.740
<i>I'll lock myself away in my room</i>

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:59.290
<b>KEEP OUT!</b>

00:15:58.740 --> 00:16:02.160
<i>and won't be able to enjoy anything 
but the internet, anime, and manga.</i>

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:04.790
<i>I can't take it anymore!</i>

00:16:02.430 --> 00:16:06.190
<i>But during those times,</i>

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:06.160
Hiromi, are you okay?

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:07.730
Are you not feeling well?

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:11.150
<i>I hope you remember this day.</i>

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:09.670
Tomo-chan...

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:16.960
<i>For the next three years, you will 
sometimes feel lost or bewildered.</i>

00:16:17.440 --> 00:16:22.070
<i>You may even feel overwhelmed by uncertainty.</i>

00:16:22.070 --> 00:16:25.130
<i>But when that time comes, look beside you.</i>

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:28.510
<i>Standing there are your 
friends who are studying</i>

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:30.960
<i>and growing alongside you at this school.</i>

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:35.020
<i>All of us are hoping that you'll experience</i>

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:40.160
<i>a fruitful academic life with the 
neighbors you just turned toward.</i>

00:16:35.530 --> 00:16:36.650
What's wrong?

00:16:38.900 --> 00:16:40.160
It's nothing.

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:44.520
<i>That's right. As far as 
friends go, I already have...</i>

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:49.730
<i>I will now introduce your homeroom teachers.</i>

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:53.560
<i>Class A's homeroom teacher 
is Ishida Mitsue-sensei.</i>

00:16:53.560 --> 00:16:56.240
<i>Class B's homeroom teacher 
is Mori Shiki-sensei.</i>

00:16:56.580 --> 00:17:00.020
She really is a teacher here.

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:02.700
And she's apparently our homeroom teacher.

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:21.470
Looks like we're finished with introductions.

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:27.440
<b>Mori
 Shiki</b>

00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:27.440
I'd like to conclude homeroom 
with a message from me.

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:34.330
As you grow from children into 
adults as high school students,

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:39.060
you'll undergo a variety of experiences,
beginning with studying together.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:43.290
I'm sure you all grew up 
in different environments.

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:46.790
There will probably be differences between 
the experiences you'll have in the future.

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:49.880
But if you begin moving forward 
according to your desires,

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:52.060
you'll find you have the freedom to go there.

00:17:52.060 --> 00:17:54.400
In other words, if you wanted to,

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:57.730
you could travel from the tip of Hokkaido 
to the southern end of Okinawa.

00:17:57.730 --> 00:18:03.010
No, if you wanted to, you have the freedom 
to cross oceans and go wherever you want.

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:12.940
<i>The freedom to go wherever we want...</i>

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:17.450
Where you go and what you do is up to you.

00:18:18.010 --> 00:18:20.340
All I can say is this.

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:23.450
I hope you have fun.

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:27.120
See, hear, experience, and eat lots of things.

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:32.540
Enjoy your three years of high school 
to the fullest, and find your own joy.

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:38.480
And hopefully, you'll experience 
that joy with friends.

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:43.100
<b>Mori
Shiki</b>

00:18:40.820 --> 00:18:42.150
I've said what I need to say.

00:18:42.150 --> 00:18:43.940
You're free to go.

00:18:48.630 --> 00:18:52.780
The freedom to go wherever 
our desires take us, huh?

00:18:52.780 --> 00:18:55.550
That teacher had some surprisingly 
good things to say.

00:18:55.550 --> 00:18:59.640
But how far will my feet take me?

00:18:59.640 --> 00:19:04.490
Whether it's by train or by plane,
 with our allowances...

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:09.000
A frail high school girl can't go far.

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:13.630
Were those bicycles?

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:15.360
They were so fast.

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:17.650
They're almost out of sight already.

00:19:17.650 --> 00:19:21.780
Yeah. There are a lot of people who 
ride bikes like that down this road.

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:23.960
They were all girls.

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:25.080
Looks like it.

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:26.530
Lucky them.

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:31.300
If I could ride like that, 
I bet I could go anywhere.

00:19:31.300 --> 00:19:38.280
Then you'd better start learning 
how to ride a bike without help.

00:19:38.590 --> 00:19:41.030
Roger that, Coach Tomo-chan.

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:44.040
Face forward! Don't wobble!

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:45.200
Okay!

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:47.040
You can do it!

00:21:22.600 --> 00:21:28.550
Come to think of it, the bike she was 
riding had training wheels on it.

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:33.100
I wonder if she was able to ride it okay.

00:21:36.130 --> 00:21:40.160
<i>The appeal of road bikes on full display 
makes you want to start riding tomorrow.</i>

