00:21:48.510 --> 00:21:50.730
<i>A-O-P's Fukuo Yui...</i>

00:21:50.730 --> 00:21:52.910
<i>And Hirose Yuki.</i>

00:21:53.810 --> 00:21:58.210
<b>Road bikes come
in a variety of
 designs and shapes</b>

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:58.210
<i>The first trap newbies fall into 
is choosing the right parts.</i>

00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:01.930
<i>"I don't know what to choose!"</i>

00:22:01.930 --> 00:22:04.480
<i>"There are too many choices!"</i>

00:22:04.480 --> 00:22:06.530
<i>"I guess we should come back later..."</i>

00:22:06.530 --> 00:22:07.760
<i>"Yeah."</i>

00:22:08.490 --> 00:22:12.100
Gloom

00:22:10.120 --> 00:22:12.670
<i>In order to make sure that 
doesn't happen to you,</i>

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:17.120
<b>Choosing a Bike 1: Choosing Based on the Frame</b>

00:22:12.670 --> 00:22:14.940
<i>we'll learn how to choose the right frame.</i>

00:22:17.120 --> 00:22:22.150
Yamada-san, this is our first 
time buying road bikes.

00:22:22.150 --> 00:22:24.860
How should we choose a bike?

00:22:22.150 --> 00:22:26.240
<b>Y's Road Ochanomizu
Manager Yamada Yunosuke-san</b>

00:22:24.860 --> 00:22:28.000
Bicycle frames are made 
of different materials,

00:22:27.300 --> 00:22:36.660
<b>Choosing a Bike
Choose the right material based on intended use</b>

00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:35.140
so it's necessary to choose a material 
appropriate for your intended use.

00:22:33.540 --> 00:22:34.690
Really?

00:22:34.690 --> 00:22:35.620
Really?

00:22:35.620 --> 00:22:39.580
The chromoly frame is well-known.

00:22:37.520 --> 00:22:45.020
<b>Chromoly</b>

00:22:39.580 --> 00:22:43.490
Chromoly frames are made from steel, 
so magnets will stick to it.

00:22:42.010 --> 00:22:42.720
Steel.

00:22:43.490 --> 00:22:47.130
The material itself is very strong.
It's very tough.

00:22:45.020 --> 00:22:47.860
<b>The material is strong and tough</b>

00:22:47.130 --> 00:22:48.830
So it's okay even if you fall?

00:22:48.830 --> 00:22:50.180
It won't break, even if you fall.

00:22:50.180 --> 00:22:51.110
Wow.

00:22:50.180 --> 00:22:56.100
<b>Chromoly: Strong and shock absorbent, but heavy.
For people who want a slow and comfortable ride.</b>

00:22:51.110 --> 00:22:56.100
I recommend this frame for people who
want to tour or ride around slowly.

00:22:56.100 --> 00:22:58.180
This frame is made of carbon.

00:22:56.100 --> 00:23:01.770
<b>Carbon</b>

00:22:58.540 --> 00:22:59.850
The carbon frame is really light.

00:22:59.850 --> 00:23:01.770
But it's so light.

00:23:01.770 --> 00:23:04.900
Because it can be strengthened 
where necessary,

00:23:01.770 --> 00:23:10.570
<b>Carbon: Strong and light, but expensive.
 For people looking for speed.</b>

00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:10.570
it's mostly chosen by people 
interested in racing.

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:12.250
Finally, there's aluminum.

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:12.910
<b>Aluminum</b>

00:23:12.250 --> 00:23:15.800
A lot of aluminum frames are affordable.

00:23:12.910 --> 00:23:20.040
<b>Aluminum: Light and sturdy, but not shock absorbent.
Recommended for beginners due to low price.</b>

00:23:15.800 --> 00:23:20.040
A lot of people choose an aluminum 
frame for their first bike.

00:23:20.040 --> 00:23:22.790
Maybe I'll get the chromoly one.

00:23:22.790 --> 00:23:24.710
You want it to last a while?

00:23:23.660 --> 00:23:27.740
Yeah. Even if I fall, with the chromoly...

00:23:27.740 --> 00:23:29.070
I bet you'd fall.

